Netzblick 0.4.1 - third-party data

1. IP Geolocation by DB-IP
   Creator: DB-IP.com / Eris Networks S.A.S.
   Dataset: IP to Country Lite, October 2026
   Source: https://db-ip.com/db/download/ip-to-country-lite
   Download: https://download.db-ip.com/free/dbip-country-lite-2026-10.csv.gz
   License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
   License text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
   Summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Changes: CSV ranges sorted and converted to a fixed-record binary index;
   no editorial modification of country assignments. Country-only lookup,
   not a city or exact location database. Attribution is also shown in the UI.
   No endorsement by DB-IP is implied. Data provided without guarantees.

2. Natural Earth
   Dataset: 1:110m Admin 0 Countries (country outlines and label coordinates)
   Source: https://www.naturalearthdata.com/downloads/110m-cultural-vectors/110m-admin-0-countries/
   Download: https://naturalearth.s3.amazonaws.com/110m_cultural/ne_110m_admin_0_countries.zip
   Terms: https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/
   License/status: public domain. No permission is needed to use the data.
   Changes: equirectangular projection into a 1000 x 500 local vector canvas;
   coordinates rounded for the UI; country labels use source label points.
   These label points do not locate servers. No endorsement is implied.

Original-input hashes and record counts are in data/manifest.json.
Development tooling (not required to run the app): Python 3 + pyshp.
The development SDKs and test-time NuGet assemblies are not redistributed.

3. ETW runtime
   Microsoft.Diagnostics.Tracing.TraceEvent 3.1.21 and dependencies.
   Source: https://github.com/microsoft/perfview
   Exact package versions and target frameworks: lib/dependencies.json
   Each package's included license is retained under lib/.
   The TraceEvent package (including its native kernel control helpers)
   is licensed under MIT. The source of the Netzblick wrapper is included.

